{title: Come, Ye Thankful People, Come}
{artist: Henry Alford / George J. Elvey}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 96}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 587장}
{title_ko: 감사하는 성도여}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Come, ye thankful [D]people, [G]come
[C]Raise the [G]song of [D]harvest [G]home
[G]All is safely [D]gathered [G]in
[C]Ere the [G]winter [D]storms be[G]gin
[G]God our Maker [D]doth pro[G]vide
[C]For our [G]wants to [D]be sup[G]plied
[G]Come to God's own [D]temple, [G]come
[C]Raise the [G]song of [D]harvest [G]home
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]All the world is [D]God's own [G]field
[C]Fruit unto His [G]praise to [D]yield
[G]Wheat and tares to[D]gether [G]sown
[C]Unto [G]joy or [D]sorrow [G]grown
[G]First the blade and [D]then the [G]ear
[C]Then the [G]full corn [D]shall ap[G]pear
[G]Lord of harvest, [D]grant that [G]we
[C]Wholesome [G]grain and [D]pure may [G]be
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]For the Lord our [D]God shall [G]come
[C]And shall [G]take His [D]harvest [G]home
[G]From His field shall [D]in that [G]day
[C]All of[G]fenses [D]purge a[G]way
[G]Give His angels [D]charge at [G]last
[C]In the [G]fire the [D]tares to [G]cast
[G]But the fruitful [D]ears to [G]store
[C]In His [G]garner [D]ever[G]more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Even so, Lord, [D]quickly [G]come
[C]Bring Thy [G]final [D]harvest [G]home
[G]Gather Thou Thy [D]people [G]in
[C]Free from [G]sorrow, [D]free from [G]sin
[G]There, forever [D]purified
[C]In Thy [G]garner [D]to a[G]bide
[G]Come, with all Thine [D]angels, [G]come
[C]Raise the [G]glorious [D]harvest [G]home
{end_of_verse}
